# VitalPet — Data Layer Conventions (drift + SQLCipher)

## Drift table definitions (source of truth)
```dart
// lib/core/database/app_database.dart
import 'package:drift/drift.dart';
import 'package:drift_flutter/drift_flutter.dart';

// check_ins — one row per check-in session
class CheckIns extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();                          // UUID PK
  TextColumn get utcDate => text()();                     // "2025-06-15" — UTC date string
  TextColumn get localDate => text()();                   // "2025-06-15" — device local date
  IntColumn get wellnessScore => integer()();             // 1–10
  IntColumn get mode => integer()();                      // 1, 2, or 3
  TextColumn get answersJson => text()();                 // JSON array of answered questions
  RealColumn get depthScore => real().withDefault(const Constant(0.0))(); // 0.0–1.0
  BoolColumn get isPartial => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();
  TextColumn get amendedAt => text().nullable()();        // ISO 8601 UTC if amended
  TextColumn get createdAt => text()();                   // ISO 8601 UTC

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}

// pet_state — single-row table (current active pet)
class PetStateTable extends Table {
  TextColumn get petId => text()();
  TextColumn get name => text()();
  TextColumn get species => text()();                     // 'cat'|'dog'|'rabbit'|'dragon'
  IntColumn get vitality => integer().withDefault(const Constant(60))();
  IntColumn get streak => integer().withDefault(const Constant(0))();
  TextColumn get lastCheckinUtc => text().nullable()();
  BoolColumn get calmMode => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();
  IntColumn get consecutiveBadDays => integer().withDefault(const Constant(0))();
  BoolColumn get freezeAvailable => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(true))();
  TextColumn get freezeLastUsedDate => text().nullable()();
  TextColumn get deletionScheduledAt => text().nullable()();
  BoolColumn get vulnerabilityCardShown => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();
  BoolColumn get vulnerabilityFrozen => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {petId};
}

// baseline_stats — rolling 14-day stats per metric
class BaselineStats extends Table {
  TextColumn get metric => text()();
  RealColumn get mean14d => real()();
  RealColumn get stddev14d => real()();
  IntColumn get sampleCount => integer()();
  TextColumn get lastComputedUtc => text()();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {metric};
}

// audit_log — append-only
class AuditLog extends Table {
  IntColumn get id => integer().autoIncrement()();
  TextColumn get eventType => text()();
  TextColumn get utcTimestamp => text()();
  TextColumn get sessionId => text().nullable()();
  TextColumn get payloadHash => text().nullable()();      // SHA-256 of content, never raw content
}

// slm_context_cache
class SlmContextCache extends Table {
  TextColumn get date => text()();                        // "2025-06-15"
  TextColumn get contextSnapshot => text()();             // pre-serialised JSON context

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {date};
}

// pet_archive — deceased pets
class PetArchive extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();
  TextColumn get name => text()();
  TextColumn get species => text()();
  IntColumn get lifespanDays => integer()();
  IntColumn get totalCheckins => integer()();
  TextColumn get topSymptom => text().nullable()();
  TextColumn get diedAtUtc => text()();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}
```

## Opening the encrypted database
```dart
// lib/core/encryption/encryption_service.dart
// Key is stored in flutter_secure_storage (backed by iOS Keychain / Android Keystore)
// and passed to drift's DriftNativeOptions.

Future<AppDatabase> openEncryptedDatabase() async {
  final key = await EncryptionService.getOrCreateKey();
  return AppDatabase(
    DriftNativeDatabase.fromKey(key), // sqlcipher_flutter_libs provides this
  );
}
// Never open a plain DriftNativeDatabase() without a key.
```

## Migration pattern
```dart
// lib/core/database/migrations/migration_v2.dart
// Add a column — always with a default value for existing rows
MigrationStrategy get migration => MigrationStrategy(
  onCreate: (m) => m.createAll(),
  onUpgrade: (m, from, to) async {
    if (from < 2) {
      await m.addColumn(petStateTable, petStateTable.vulnerabilityCardShown);
      await m.addColumn(petStateTable, petStateTable.vulnerabilityFrozen);
    }
  },
);
// Never drop or rename columns — add new ones with defaults.
```

## Atomic writes — always use transactions
```dart
// CORRECT — all check-in writes in one transaction
await db.transaction(() async {
  await checkInDao.insertCheckIn(sessionCompanion);
  await petDao.updateVitality(newVitality, newStreak);
  await auditLogDao.append(AuditEvent.checkinWrite(
    sessionId: sessionCompanion.id.value,
    payloadHash: _sha256(sessionCompanion.answersJson.value),
  ));
  // Post-commit: baseline tracker runs as a follow-up after transaction closes
});
```

## Timestamp discipline
- All stored timestamps: ISO 8601 UTC strings `"2025-06-15T14:30:00.000Z"` — use `DateTime.now().toUtc().toIso8601String()`
- `utcDate`: `"2025-06-15"` — used for streak calculation (prevents timezone-shift breaks)
- `localDate`: device local date — used for display calendar
- Never store `millisecondsSinceEpoch` integers

## AuditLogDao — append only
```dart
class AuditLogDao extends DatabaseAccessor<AppDatabase> {
  // ONLY public methods:
  Future<void> append(AuditEvent event) async { ... }
  Future<void> appendInTransaction(AuditEvent event) async { ... } // call inside db.transaction()
  // No update(), no delete(), no clear()
}

// Required audit event types (use AuditEvent.xxx() factories):
// checkinWrite, amendment, filterTrigger, handoffExport, dataExport, deleteInitiated
```

## Deletion flow
```dart
// Step 1: schedule (7-day recovery window)
await petDao.setDeletionScheduled(DateTime.now().toUtc().toIso8601String());
await auditLogDao.append(AuditEvent.deleteInitiated());

// Step 2: on next launch, check if 7 days have passed
final scheduled = await petDao.getDeletionScheduledAt();
if (scheduled != null && DateTime.now().difference(DateTime.parse(scheduled)).inDays >= 7) {
  await EncryptionService.destroyKey(); // removes from flutter_secure_storage
  // DB is now cryptographically inaccessible — app shows first-launch screen
}
```

## JSON export
`lib/core/database/export_service.dart` — exported JSON must:
- Include all tables EXCEPT `audit_log` (internal) and `slm_context_cache` (reconstructable)
- Be pretty-printed: `const JsonEncoder.withIndent('  ')`
- Include `exportedAt: DateTime.now().toUtc().toIso8601String()` at root
- Never include the encryption key or any cryptographic material
